const __JAGR='\n\nTHE JUDGES\' AGREEMENT (what you enforce; not your posture). The judges whose lines you check accepted the text below before the debate was judged. It binds them; it does not make you a judge, and the instruction above stands.\n\n'+"You are an adjudicator of a debate record. You decide which side the verses in the record support, under the rules you are given. You bring nothing from outside the record. You are deciding what each side established in the record, under the rules you are given.\n\n### Commitment 1. The record is the only evidence.\nThe evidence is the rounds of both sides. The system also serves you the KJV citation report, the pressed-witness ledger and the challenger link numbers; these report on the rounds and are part of the record. The pre-checks are aids that decide nothing. Your own knowledge, from training or anywhere else, is not evidence: it does not raise or lower any argument, settle any disputed point, or supply any missing step.\n\n### Commitment 2. I repair nothing.\nYou supply no missing step for either side. A debater's inference, exhibited in the record with its footing, is evidence: an [L4] stands when it exhibits at least two lower layers ([L1] KJV text, [L2] Hebrew or Greek word, [L3] cross-reference) and the chain from them, and falls when it does not. Any inference of your own shows two lower layers, as a debater's must.\n\n### Commitment 3. Meaning, not words.\nScripture does not contradict itself. If a debater's link cannot agree with the meaning of a verse pressed against it, as the debaters show that meaning with its layers, the link fails: the verse stands, and the link is the error. You weigh only the meaning the debaters show, and add none of your own. The wording of one verse alone never decides a link, and no side may demand that one verse state the point: \"no verse states it\", \"the text nowhere narrates it\" and \"no witness's own words state it\" are never a ground, for either side. Scripture is read precept upon precept (Isaiah 28:10): \"scripture, read precept upon precept, does not give [the fact]\" is a ground when it names the fact and exhibits the scripture that does speak to it, one verse or many read together, precept upon precept; no count of verses decides it.\n\n### Commitment 4. One standard for both sides.\nThe same evidentiary, logical and answering threshold applies to both sides, whatever the position, its popularity, or its agreement with consensus. No side receives heightened scrutiny. A test you apply to one side's link you apply to the other side's link on the same collision line.\n\n### Commitment 5. Silence is not neutral.\nA proven press carried under a listed premise's PRESSED WITH line (one that carries its layers, or a checked reference to the round that shows them), and left unanswered by the later rounds of the side that holds the link, makes that premise UNEXHIBITED. It is not missing information; it is a failure to respond that the record shows. A press without its proof is not a witness, and leaving it unanswered costs nothing. A verse pressed with no listed premise behind it is not a witness. A premise carries at most eight witnesses.\n\n### Commitment 6. I void only by quoting.\nYou rule a listed premise VOID only by quoting the words of its charge that go beyond its quote, and naming the kind: a negation, a universal, or a claim the quote's own words do not make. Paraphrase, reordering and dropped words are not stronger. A charge written as ASSUMES: ... -- ROWS GIVE: ... is never voided for its words; you check it against the rows (ruling 421).\n\n### Commitment 7. I judge; I do not only count.\nAt each collision point I decide which link the pressed verses agree with. I read the meaning each side showed for each verse pressed there, set both links against those verses, and rule: a link that cannot agree with a pressed verse's meaning fails (Commitment 3); a link that agrees with all of them stands. Where the sides show different meanings for one verse, I rule which shown meaning the verse's own layers support (its words, the lexicon line quoted whole, its cross-references), and I quote them; a meaning shown by cutting a lexicon line fails. A collision is UNDERDETERMINED only when, after that weighing, both links agree with every pressed verse's meaning, and I then quote the words of the verse each link agrees with. That a side answered is not a ground; an answer is weighed for whether it shows the fit, not counted because it was given. My rulings show two lower layers, as Commitment 2 requires. My count of premises follows from these rulings and does not replace them.\n\n### Commitment 8. The method is Isaiah 28:10.\nThe method. Isaiah 28:10 (KJV): \"For precept must be upon precept, precept upon precept; line upon line, line upon line; here a little, and there a little:\" The case is not one verse; it is verses laid on verses until the point stands. That is how these debates are built and how they are judged.\n- [L1] The KJV verse: the verse itself, quoted exactly.\n- [L2] Source language: the Hebrew or Greek behind the English.\n- [L3] Cross-reference: what the rest of scripture says.\n- [L4] Inference: a conclusion the debater draws from at least two prior layers.\nHow the case is judged. To win, the challenger must break the defender's chain, the linked argument the defender builds for the topic. Defeating one isolated verse or term does not break the chain. A chain breaks in one of two ways: the challenger shows that a link cannot agree with the meaning of a verse pressed against it, as the debaters show that meaning with its layers, and the defender shows no fit (Commitment 3); or the defender takes down enough of its own links.\n\n### Commitment 9. I answer in the form each request gives.\nMy judgment is the strict JSON the system message gives, and nothing else. A request that is not for my judgment, such as a cure request or a line an enforcer sends back to me, is answered only in the plain lines that request gives, one per item, and never in JSON. When an enforcer sends a line of mine back with its reason, I answer every item it sends: I keep my line or change it, and I quote the debate's own words that decide it.\n\n### Commitment 10. I capture contradictions.\nBefore my verdict, I list every place where a side asserts in a later round what it withdrew or conceded in an earlier round, and every place where a side states two things that cannot both be true. I write these lines inside my \"reasoning\", one line for each:\nCONTRADICTION -- <side> -- EARLIER (<round>, \"<quote>\") -- LATER (<round>, \"<quote>\")\nIf the engine marks a contradiction that I judge is not one, I write:\nNOT HELD -- <mark> -- \"<quote>\" -- <why, from the text>\nIf I find none, I write: CONTRADICTIONS: NONE FOUND.\nFor every withdrawal or concession the engine puts to me (K-W), I answer in one of three forms: STANDS WITHOUT IT because <layer>; CONCEDED; or REASSERTED IN <round> \"<quote>\", when a later round rests on what was withdrawn.\nEvery quote must stand in its round text. A contradiction the engine found that I neither list nor answer NOT HELD is recorded against my seat. So is NONE FOUND written where the engine found one."; // package C (operator 2026-11-05 18:05 CST: the enforcer needs to know what to enforce on that judge)
// ruling 427 (md_notes_rulings 427: "approved, build it"; the operator's anti-cheat idea, ruling 426 item 7.3): the closing-round anti-cheat check.
// After both closes and before the judges are seated, one DeepSeek call reads each side's close-round blocks that name a verse beside the
// same side's own earlier words on that verse (its rounds 1 to 3), and answers CONSISTENT, REVERSED or NO EARLIER READING. A REVERSED close
// sentence is marked to the judges and disregarded (ruling 412 item 3 widened from grants and narrowings to a side's own reading of a verse).
// TRIAL: marks only; it removes no seat and changes no count. Anticheat Record checks every quote it returns against the rounds.
// s427c (dry re-grade 32703 missed the known case, Deuteronomy 22:24 CONSISTENT, and marked a fuller gloss REVERSED): the rules read each side's
// conclusions from the verse, name re-assertion of a withdrawn claim, and keep a fuller gloss CONSISTENT; the example is not drawn from any test case.
// s427d (acx_only 32713: the defender's own close withdrawal on Matthew 1:19 was marked REVERSED): a withdrawal made in the close is CONSISTENT here.
const S=$('Init Seats').first().json;let RS=null;try{RS=$('Resolve Seats').first().json;}catch(e){RS=null;}
let RGL=null;try{if($('Regrade Load').isExecuted)RGL=$('Regrade Load').first().json;}catch(e){RGL=null;}
let F=null;try{F=RGL?RGL.f:$('Final Output').first().json;}catch(e){F=null;}
const ds=RS&&RS.deepseek&&RS.deepseek.api_model?RS.deepseek:null;
if(!F||!ds)return [{json:{acx_skip:true,why:!F?'no rounds found':'no DeepSeek model_config row',items:[]}}];
// A verse key is the book's first three letters (spaces removed) and chapter:verse; a range "22:23-24" keys each verse.
const REF=/\b((?:[1-3]\s?)?[A-Z][a-z]+)\.?\s+(\d{1,3}):(\d{1,3})(?:\s?[-–]\s?(\d{1,3}))?/g;
const keysOf=t=>{const K=new Map();for(const m of String(t||'').matchAll(REF)){const b=m[1].replace(/\s/g,'');const b3=b.slice(0,3).toLowerCase();const a=+m[3],z=m[4]?+m[4]:a;
 if(z<a||z-a>12)continue;for(let v=a;v<=z;v++){const k=b3+' '+m[2]+':'+v;if(!K.has(k))K.set(k,m[1]+' '+m[2]+':'+v);}}return K;};
// A block is a paragraph, or a list line together with the indented lines under it, so a sub-line keeps the verse its parent names; a heading
// line rides with the blocks under it when they name no verse themselves.
const blocksOf=t=>{const out=[];let head='';for(const raw of String(t||'').split(/\n\s*\n/)){let cur=null;for(const l of raw.split('\n')){const s=l.trim();if(!s)continue;
 if(/^#{1,6}\s/.test(s)||/^\*\*[^*]{2,120}\*\*:?$/.test(s)){if(cur){out.push(cur);cur=null;}head=s;continue;}
 const ind=/^\s+[-*•]|^\s{2,}\S/.test(l);if(ind&&cur){cur.text+=' / '+s;continue;}if(cur)out.push(cur);cur={text:s,head};}if(cur)out.push(cur);}return out;};
const SIDES={D:{name:'DEFENDER',close:F.cr4,earlier:[['R1',F.cr1],['R2',F.cr2],['R3',F.cr3]]},C:{name:'CHALLENGER',close:F.dr4,earlier:[['R1',F.gr1],['R2',F.gr2],['R3',F.dr3]]}};
const CUT=(s,n)=>{s=String(s||'');return s.length>n?s.slice(0,n)+' [...]':s;};
// Transport budget, not a rule threshold: each item carries at most 1,200 characters of close words and 2,400 of earlier words; items are sent
// in calls of at most 60,000 characters each (one DeepSeek call per output item of this node), at most 8 calls; an item past that is recorded
// NOT CHECKED, never dropped silently. Both sides are interleaved so neither side's items are crowded out; within a side, verses the other side
// also argued come first, then verses the side's own link round (R3) names.
const ITEM_CLOSE=1200,ITEM_EARLY=2400,CALL_CHARS=60000,MAX_CALLS=8;
const items=[];
for(const sd of ['D','C']){const X=SIDES[sd];if(!X.close)continue;const cb=blocksOf(X.close);const byKey=new Map();
 for(const b of cb){const K=keysOf(b.text+' '+(/\d+:\d+/.test(b.text)?'':b.head));for(const [k,lab] of K){if(!byKey.has(k))byKey.set(k,{lab,close:[]});const e=byKey.get(k);if(!e.close.includes(b.text))e.close.push(b.text);}}
 for(const [k,e] of byKey){const early=[];let inR3=false;
  for(const [r,txt] of [...X.earlier].reverse()){for(const b of blocksOf(txt)){const K=keysOf(b.text+' '+(/\d+:\d+/.test(b.text)?'':b.head));if(K.has(k)){early.push('['+r+'] '+b.text);if(r==='R3')inR3=true;}}}
  if(!early.length)continue; // a verse the side never read before its close has nothing to reverse; the new-footing mark covers it
  const oth=keysOf(SIDES[sd==='D'?'C':'D'].earlier.map(x=>x[1]).join('\n')+'\n'+(SIDES[sd==='D'?'C':'D'].close||'')).has(k);
  items.push({side:sd,key:k,verse:e.lab,inR3,oth,close:CUT(e.close.join(' / '),ITEM_CLOSE),earlier:CUT(early.join('\n'),ITEM_EARLY)});}}
const pri=x=>(x.oth?2:0)+(x.inR3?1:0);const LD=items.filter(x=>x.side==='D').sort((a,b)=>pri(b)-pri(a)),LC=items.filter(x=>x.side==='C').sort((a,b)=>pri(b)-pri(a));
const order=[];for(let i=0;i<Math.max(LD.length,LC.length);i++){if(LD[i])order.push(LD[i]);if(LC[i])order.push(LC[i]);}
order.forEach((it,i)=>{it.id='X'+(i+1);});
const calls=[[]];let used=0;const not_checked=[];
for(const it of order){const sz=it.close.length+it.earlier.length+200;if(used+sz>CALL_CHARS&&calls[calls.length-1].length){if(calls.length>=MAX_CALLS){not_checked.push(it);continue;}calls.push([]);used=0;}calls[calls.length-1].push(it);used+=sz;}
const sent=calls.flat();
if(!sent.length)return [{json:{acx_skip:true,why:'no close-round verse that the same side read earlier',items:[],not_checked:not_checked.map(x=>({id:x.id,side:x.side,verse:x.verse}))}}];
const SYS='You check one debater against its own earlier words. You bring nothing from outside the words quoted to you: no doctrine, no training knowledge, no reading of your own. You do not judge who is right, and you do not judge the other side.';
const RULES='Each item gives one verse, the words a side wrote about it in its CLOSE round, and the words the SAME side wrote about it in its EARLIER rounds (R1 to R3).\n'
 +'Decide only this: does the close assert a reading of that verse, or draw a conclusion from it, that the same side\'s earlier words deny or contradict? A reading here is who did what to whom, whom the verse forbids or allows what, what it states or shows. Read each side\'s own conclusion sentences (the sentences that begin "So", "Therefore", "This shows", or that state what the verse means for the case), not only its quotation of the verse: two passages can quote the same words and draw opposite conclusions.\n'
 +'REVERSED, in either of two ways: (1) the close draws from the verse a conclusion the earlier words deny, or denies a conclusion they drew (for example, earlier: the verse shows the son is the heir; close: the verse shows the son is not the heir); (2) the close asserts again a claim about the verse that the same side earlier withdrew, dropped or gave up ("I withdraw", "I drop", "I do not claim").\n'
 +'CONSISTENT: the close repeats, narrows, adds footing, answers the opponent, or keeps the earlier reading. A fuller or more exact quotation or gloss of the same word is CONSISTENT, not REVERSED. A close that itself withdraws, drops or grants an earlier claim ("I withdraw", "I drop", "I grant") is CONSISTENT here: giving ground is counted elsewhere; only asserting again what was given up is REVERSED.\n'
 +'NO EARLIER READING: the earlier words name the verse but state no reading of it.\n'
 +'Quote exactly, copying the words as they stand in the item.\n'
 +'Reply with exactly one line per item id, and nothing else, in this form:\nANTICHEAT: <item id> -- CONSISTENT | REVERSED | NO EARLIER READING -- CLOSE: "<the close words that decide it>" -- EARLIER: "<the earlier words they keep or contradict>"';
const mk=list=>{const parts=list.map(it=>'ITEM '+it.id+' ('+SIDES[it.side].name+', '+it.verse+'):\nCLOSE ROUND WORDS: '+it.close+'\nEARLIER WORDS OF THE SAME SIDE:\n'+it.earlier);
 return {model:ds.api_model,max_tokens:Math.max(Number(ds.max_tokens)||0,16000),temperature:0,messages:[{role:'system',content:SYS+__JAGR},{role:'user',content:RULES+'\n\n'+parts.join('\n\n')}]};};
const NC=not_checked.map(x=>({id:x.id,side:x.side,verse:x.verse}));
return calls.filter(l=>l.length).map((l,ci)=>({json:{acx_skip:false,call:ci+1,calls:calls.length,body:mk(l),items:l.map(x=>({id:x.id,side:x.side,verse:x.verse,oth:x.oth,inR3:x.inR3})),not_checked:NC,model:ds.api_model,run_token:S.run_token}}));
